renovate: merge nothing while BURROW_RENOVATE_NO_MERGE is set

burrow's own, not upstream's. renovate-run (crates/burrow-renovate) sets it
for a repository whose landing isn't the steward's (burrow-landing's record):
there only conaryd moves the trunk, and Renovate only opens and updates PRs.

Forcing `automerge: false` isn't enough. A security fix's package rule
carries its own `force` (vulnerabilityAlerts, which turns automerge on), and
so can a repository's config, and either outranks the run's. So each way
Renovate merges asks one switch in its own environment, which no
repository's config reaches: a PR's merge (and its automerge comment), a
branch's merge onto its base (held, the branch gets a PR instead), and
the platform's own automerge, at a PR's creation or its reattempt.

